== 9. How to read this =========================================
  RASSF9 verdict: INTERMEDIATE

  If INTERMEDIATE or UNMETHYLATED: the RASSF9 promoter is not uniformly
  silenced by methylation in melanoma cells, yet the gene is off. Promoter
  methylation is therefore not sufficient to explain its absence from the
  malignant compartment, and the TCGA correlation is more plausibly driven
  by the compartments that express RASSF9 at all. That is a result, not a
  failure, and it is the honest answer to whether the relationship holds
  'within melanoma cells'.

  If HYPERMETHYLATED: consistent with the TCGA direction. Note it still
  does not demonstrate a methylation-expression relationship in lines,
  because there is no expression variance to relate it to.

  LIMITATIONS to carry into the write-up:
   1. Cell lines are not tumours. Cultured lines drift epigenetically,
      and global hypermethylation is common in long-passage lines.
   2. 56 of 154 DepMap melanoma models matched a GDSC sample by name.
      Most of the rest are absent from the GDSC panel, but some may be
      name-spelling losses.
   3. Methylation (GDSC/Sanger) and expression (DepMap) come from
      different laboratories and different cell stocks.
   4. No correlation is reported, by design, because expression has no
      usable variance in these lines.
